## 2. What's in the repo

### `firmware/warivo-node/warivo-node.ino` — the node

290 lines of Arduino + NimBLE. Advertises as **`Warivo-Node`** and exposes one GATT
service, `fff0`:

| Characteristic | Direction | Payload |
| --- | --- | --- |
| `fff1` telemetry | node → phone, NOTIFY at 5 Hz | `{v, soc, spd, odo, a, w, rng, tout, tbat, dist, up}` |
| `fff2` gps | phone → node, WRITE | `{lat, lon, spd, ts}` |
| `fff3` config | phone → node, WRITE | `{beep, beep_cm}` |

Configured for the reference scooter: lead-acid 60 V (5 × 12 V, 30 Ah), 65.0 V full /
52.5 V empty, wheel circumference 1.47 m (90/90-12). **Change those four constants for a
different scooter** — they are the only scooter-specific values.

`USE_CURRENT` and `HAS_DIST_SENSOR` are both `false` until you wire those sensors.

### `android/warivo-launcher/` — the head unit

Native Kotlin + Jetpack Compose. `minSdk 28` (Android 9), `targetSdk 29` (Android 10),
`compileSdk 34`. 20 source files, ~2,900 lines. Registers as `CATEGORY_HOME`, so it is a
real launcher, not a full-screen app.

Five panels behind a bottom dock: **Drive** (gauges), **Map**, **Music**, **Search**,
**Setup**.

Chosen over the alternatives on purpose: Open Launcher's `minSdk` is unconfirmed for API 29
and its widget-grid architecture isn't what we want; Flutter would still need hand-written
Kotlin for Device Owner, Lock Task and forcing the radios on — native code *plus* a bridge
instead of just native code.

**Nothing depends on Play Services**, anywhere. Location is `LocationManager`, not
FusedLocationProvider, because the Path B ROM ships without GApps — so the same APK drops
straight into it.

### `audit.md` — the optional signal taps

Feasibility study for reading throttle %, gear, headlight, high beam, parking light,
indicators and reverse off the loom. All read-only taps in parallel; nothing is cut and no
line is driven. **Blocked on a five-minute multimeter session** — §4 has the checklist.

The launcher already renders every one of these fields and hides the ones the node isn't
sending, so when the taps land, no app change is needed.

### `branding/`

Warivo mark and logo (SVG) plus boot-animation art. The launcher's palette and icon are
derived from `warivo-mark.svg`: Deep Space Blue `#05102A` / `#0B1E45`, Celestial Aqua
`#5FF0DE` as the only accent, amber and red reserved for warnings.

